**Lemma.** Powers of $\mathbb{O}$ are injective.

**Proof.** Let $I$ be any index set and let

$$
D = \mathbb{O}^I
$$

be the Cartesian power of the two-point space $\mathbb{O}$ with the product topology. Each factor $\mathbb{O}$ is injective by **1.2**. By **1.3**, the product of injective spaces is injective under the product topology, so $D$ is injective. $\square$

**Proposition 1.5** applies this lemma with $I = \mathfrak{O}$, the open subsets of the given $T_0$-space.
